@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.819 = private unnamed_addr constant [617 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for imports that use non-standard naming conventions, like\0A`import tensorflow.keras.backend as K`.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AConsistency is good. Avoid using a non-standard naming convention for\0Aimports, and, in particular, choosing import aliases that violate PEP 8.\0A\0AFor example, aliasing via `import tensorflow.keras.backend as K` violates\0Athe guidance of PEP 8, and is thus avoided in some projects.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Aimport tensorflow.keras.backend as K\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Aimport tensorflow as tf\0A\0Atf.keras.backend\0A```\0A\0A## Options\0A- `lint.flake8-import-conventions.banned-aliases`\0A", align 1
