@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.839 = private unnamed_addr constant [917 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for uses of `typing.NoReturn` (and `typing_extensions.NoReturn`) for\0Aparameter annotations.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0APrefer `Never` over `NoReturn` for parameter annotations. `Never` has a\0Aclearer name in these contexts, since it makes little sense to talk about a\0Aparameter annotation \22not returning\22.\0A\0AThis is a purely stylistic lint: the two types have identical semantics for\0Atype checkers. Both represent Python's \22[bottom type]\22 (a type that has no\0Amembers).\0A\0A## Example\0A```pyi\0Afrom typing import NoReturn\0A\0Adef foo(x: NoReturn): ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```pyi\0Afrom typing import Never\0A\0Adef foo(x: Never): ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: `typing.Never`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.Never)\0A- [Python documentation: `typing.NoReturn`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/typing.html#typing.NoReturn)\0A\0A[bottom type]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bottom_type\0A", align 1
