@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.850 = private unnamed_addr constant [637 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for quoted type annotations in stub (`.pyi`) files, which should be avoided.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AStub files natively support forward references in all contexts, as stubs\0Aare never executed at runtime. (They should be thought of as \22data files\22\0Afor type checkers and IDEs.) As such, quotes are never required for type\0Aannotations in stub files, and should be omitted.\0A\0A## Example\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef function() -> \22int\22: ...\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A\0A```pyi\0Adef function() -> int: ...\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Typing documentation - Writing and Maintaining Stub Files](https://typing.python.org/en/latest/guides/writing_stubs.html)\0A", align 1
