@anon.879c592214345ca999bafaa324406990.858 = private unnamed_addr constant [835 x i8] c"## What it does\0AChecks for `return` statements in `try`-`except` and `finally` blocks.\0A\0A## Why is this bad?\0AThe `return` statement in a `finally` block will always be executed, even if\0Aan exception is raised in the `try` or `except` block. This can lead to\0Aunexpected behavior.\0A\0A## Example\0A```python\0Adef squared(n):\0A    try:\0A        sqr = n**2\0A        return sqr\0A    except Exception:\0A        return \22An exception occurred\22\0A    finally:\0A        return -1  # Always returns -1.\0A```\0A\0AUse instead:\0A```python\0Adef squared(n):\0A    try:\0A        return_value = n**2\0A    except Exception:\0A        return_value = \22An exception occurred\22\0A    finally:\0A        return_value = -1\0A    return return_value\0A```\0A\0A## References\0A- [Python documentation: Defining Clean-up Actions](https://docs.python.org/3/tutorial/errors.html#defining-clean-up-actions)\0A", align 1
